    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "A hotel has 17 rooms on each floor. If the hotel consists of three buildings, each with 27 floors, how many rooms are there in the hotel?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "1377 rooms",
      "worked": "There are $3\\times27=81$ floors altogether.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}81\\times17&=81\\times(10+7)\\\\81\\times17&=810+567\\\\81\\times17&=1377\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe hotel has 1377 rooms.",
